x}(xy)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2x+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y-2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ (2x+y)+(x-2y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2x+y}{x-2y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent at the point $(0,\\,1)$ is then given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}_{(0,\\,1)} \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{2x+y}{x-2y})}_{(0,\\,1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\cdot 0+1}{0-2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{0+1}{0-2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255786 1017 #edb/ref 17592186255787 13194139533856 true] [17592186255786 1089 "q-108367" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255786 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533856 true] [17592186255786 1100 "Given that ${y}^{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y)-2{x}^{2}=5,$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255786 1113 #uuid "8b9a674f-4b08-56bb-b862-861e9645fdbf" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255786 1145 "First, we differentiate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y)-2{x}^{2} & =5 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y)-2{x}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y))-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})-4x & =0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we solve the equation for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}(3{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)) & =4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4x}{3{y}^{2}-\\operatornam