rue] [17592186255851 1034 "\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)}{y+1}" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255851 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533856 true] [17592186255851 1111 #uuid "7bd8fba3-a903-566d-bf59-729f7b7d6d68" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255852 1034 "\\frac{3{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)}{2y+1}" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255852 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533856 true] [17592186255852 1111 #uuid "d407e01e-6222-578b-9e62-de7cdb3f20ee" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255853 1034 "\\frac{3\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)}{y+1}" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255853 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533856 true] [17592186255853 1111 #uuid "33890605-e540-54b0-9ad0-fdb5fc10f532" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255854 1034 "\\frac{3\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)}{3y+1}" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255854 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533856 true] [17592186255854 1111 #uuid "713ee965-7ec0-524f-9b6c-ce09bdf6c151" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255855 1034 "\\frac{3{cot}^{2}⁡(3x)}{2y+1}" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255855 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533856 true] [17592186255855 1111 #uuid "7d63c64f-4384-54c3-85ff-160f261a17c6" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255856 1017 #edb/ref 17592186255857 13194139533856 true] [17592186255856 1089 "q-341915" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255856 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533856 true] [17592186255856 1100 "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent at the point $(16,\\,4)$ for the curve $\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}=6.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255856 1113 #uuid "50d30d9c-6ebb-56fa-a396-2394eb5e50c7" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255856 1145 "To find the slope at a point, we use implicit differentiation to calculate the derivative of the curve, assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2}+{y}^{1/2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}) & =-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}) & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent at the point $(16,\\,4)$ is then given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(16,\\,4)} \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{\\sqrt{x}})|}_{(16,\\,4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{4}}{\\sqrt{16}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255857 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255858 13194139533856 true] [17592186255857 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533856 true] [17592186255857 1041 "field-1" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255857 1104 #edb/ref 17592186255858 13194139533856 true] [17592186255857 1110 #uuid "b95b92a0-3109-5324-bf41-0b1c873f9cef" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255858 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255858 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533856 true] [17592186255858 1111 #uuid "f5e87ee5-0c4a-5cfb-8b64-a340535c826d" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255859 1017 #edb/ref 17592186255860 13194139533856 true] [17592186255859 1017 #edb/ref 17592186255862 13194139533856 true] [17592186255859 1089 "q-342321" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255859 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533856 true] [17592186255859 1100 "The equation of a curve is ${x}^{2}+xy=6{y}^{2}.$ The normal line at the point $(2,1)$ intersects the $y$-axis at the point $P.$ What are the coordinates of $P?$\n\nThe coordinates of $P$ are $($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255859 1113 #uuid "2bec85f4-6642-5907-9fd0-41128942f8dd" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255859 1145 "First of all, we need to find the slope of the normal line at the point $(2,1).$ Remember that the slope of the normal line, ${m}^{′},$ is the negative reciprocal of the slope of the tangent line:\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we will calculate the derivative using implicit differentiation, assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\nNote that to differentiate the $xy$ term, we will need to use the product rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+xy & =6{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+xy) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{y}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xy) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{y}^{2}) \\\\ 2x+(y+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}) & =12y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ 2x+y+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =12y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-12y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x-y \\\\ (x-12y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x-y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{-2x-y}{x-12y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at the point $(2,1)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,\\,1)} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{-2x-y}{x-12y})|}_{(2,\\,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2(2)-1}{2-12(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-5)}{(-10)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{2})}=-2.\n$$\n\nWe can write the equation of the normal at the point $(2,1)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & ={m}^{′}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =-2(x-2) \\\\ y-1 & =-2x+4 \\\\ y & =-2x+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to find where this normal line intersects the $y$-axis. At the point $P$ the $x$-coordinate is $0,$ so we set $x=0$ and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+5 \\\\ y & =-2(0)+5 \\\\ y & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(0,\\,5).$" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255860 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255861 13194139533856 true] [17592186255860 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533856 true] [17592186255860 1041 "field-1" 13194139533856 true] [17592186255860 1104 #edb/ref 175921862